  "note": "customer: start only when the customer asks to dispute one or more debit card transactions. This includes a customer who, during a transaction review in another job, denies a transaction and agrees when the agent advises filing a dispute. Such reviews are a chip/CVV mismatch, a fraud alert, or the PIN lock investigation's check for successful unauthorized transactions on a card that cannot be unlocked.\n\nFile one dispute for each transaction the customer names. Card actions (a freeze, or a close and reissue) are not optional offers: they follow from the categories of the disputes actually filed, as the dispute procedure requires. A dispute held back by the open-dispute limit, or dropped by the customer after a record check, sets no card action.\n\nIf the customer opens by asking for a human agent, offer to help first, as the policy says, and transfer only on the 4th request."
